{\pard\plain \s0\ql\sb60\sa60\f0\fs22\ql\sb50\sa50\cbpat11 {\f11\fs14\cf4 1. For rows where the number of participants in each analysis set is presented, base the number of participants on applicable participant treatment grouping (eg, use TRTxxP for the ITT Analysis Set or the FAS Analysis Set row and TRTxxA for the Safety Analysis Set or the PK Analysis Set row). Add rows to include all analysis sets specified in the SAP. Use the [ITT][Full] Analysis Set and TRTxxP for the denominator in studies where the [ITT][Full] Analysis Set is the primary efficacy analysis set; otherwise, use the Safety Analysis Set and TRTxxA.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 2. Reasons for Premature Discontinuation should match the study eCRF. As a default, categories with all zeros are omitted. When it adds value, all categories as listed on the eCRF may be displayed, including categories with all zeros.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 3. Only display "Reason for [Premature] Discontinuation of [Any] Study [Drug] [Treatment]" section if any participants discontinued study drug. Only display "Reason for [Premature] Study Discontinuation" section if any participants discontinued the study.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 4. "Continuing Study [Drug][Treatment]", "Continuing Study", and completion at specific time points may be added for interim analyses.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 5. Denominator for categories under a treatment phase should be the number of participants who entered the respective treatment phase.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 6. Sort the reasons for premature discontinuation by descending frequency under the total column. If the frequency is tied, then sort by alphabetical order.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 7. The annotations of 'TRTxxP(N)', 'TRTxxA(N)', 'AREL(N)' and other similar ones in the tables and listings indicate that either the character (eg, TRTxxP, AREL) or the numeric (eg, TRTxxPN, ARELN) variable can be used to create the column or row.}\par}
