{\pard\plain \s0\ql\sb60\sa60\f0\fs22\ql\sb50\sa50\cbpat11 {\f11\fs14\cf4 1. This table shell can be applied based on}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226? IRC/INV assessment (PFS)}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226? ITT/FAS/PP analysis set}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226? Subgroup analysis}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226? Sensitivity analysis}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226? Unstratified/stratified analysis}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 2. There may be different categories under \u8220?Number (%) of participants censored\u8221? depending on specific study specifications. Zero rows in the pre-defined categories will be shown.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 3. Refer to study statistician\u8217?s definition on the event/censoring rules, and also the censored categories based on different endpoints and analysis.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 4. For HR and its 95% CI, please use the same parameter for number of decimal digits. If no values set for the parameter, please display 2 decimal digits by default.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 5. For survival rates and its 95% CI, please use the same parameter for number of decimal digits. If no values set for the parameter, please display 3 decimal digits by default.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 6. For median, Q1, Q3, and the corresponding 95% CI, please use the same parameter for number of decimal digits. If no values set for the parameter, please display 1 decimal digit.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 7. Line \u8220?P value (Non-Inferiority Test)\u8221? is optional for the non-inferiority study. In that case, the next line for P value from the superiority test will be displayed only if the non-inferiority test is rejected.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 8. If there are multiple treatment groups, in general, the pairwise treatment comparison will be conducted by only including the treatment groups which are compared with, unless otherwise specified by SAP. For example, if the comparison is for treatment A and B, then data from treatment group C will be excluded when doing the comparison.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 9. The duration of OS/PFS follow-up only applies to the whole analysis set, not the sub-group analysis set.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 10. The formula for calculating OS/PFS and the duration of OS/PFS follow-up are the same at individual participant level. At study level, the duration of OS follow-up is calculated using summary statistics (n, mean, std, median, Q1, Q3, minimum and maximum).}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 11. The reasons listed under \u8220?number of participants censored\u8221? should be mutually exclusive and modified based on the endpoint (PFS or OS) being analyzed and the type of analysis (primary or sensitivity). In the table template, the reasons for censoring for the primary analysis of the endpoint (PFS or OS) are listed.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 Sample Code:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226?  For stratified log-rank test:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 ods output HomTests =\u123?logrank\u125?;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 proc lifetest data=\u123?indata\u125?  outsurv=\u123?_surv\u125? timelist=xx reduceout;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      time \u123?SurTime\u125?*\u123?Censored(1)\u125?;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      strata \u123?strata1\u125? \u123?strata2\u125?/ group=\u123?trtgrp\u125? diff=all test=logrank;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 run;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 ods output close;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226?  For Un-stratified log-rank test and KM estimates at time points:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 ods output  HomTests =\u123?logrank\u125?;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 proc lifetest data=\u123?indata\u125?   outsurv=\u123?_surv\u125? timelist=xx reduceout;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      time \u123?SurTime\u125?*\u123?Censored(1)\u125?;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      strata \u123?trtgrp\u125? / diff=all test=logrank;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 run;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 ods output close;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4   \u8226?  Hazard ratio:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 ods output HazardRatios=\u123?hr\u125? estimates=\u123?test\u125?;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 proc phreg data=\u123?indata\u125?;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      class \u123?trtgrp\u125? (ref = "\u123?B\u125?"); /*specify the reference arm in (ref=\u8217?\u8217?)*/}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      strata \u123?strata1\u125? \u123?strata2\u125?; /*only needed for stratified test*/}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      model \u123?SurTime\u125?*\u123?Censored(1)\u125?=\u123?trtgrp\u125? / rl alpha=0.05 ties=efron;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      hazardratio \u123?trtgrp\u125? / alpha=0.05 diff=ref;}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4      estimate \u123?trtgrp\u125? \u123?1\u125? / testvalue=Ln_HR0; /*only needed for non-inferiority test. \u8220?estimate \u123?trtgrp\u125? 1\u8221? assigns 1 as the coefficient to be applied to the non-inferiority statistical test assign Ln_HR0=ln(HR0) where HR0 is the non-inferiority test boundary*/}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 run;}\par}
