{\pard\plain \s0\ql\sb60\sa60\f0\fs22\qc\sb50\sa200 {\f11\fs14\cf4 Table 15.11.2.1.1 Treatment-Emergent Adverse Events: Overall Summary [Default Layout 1],[Required]}\par}
{\pard\plain \s0\ql\sb60\sa60\f0\fs22\ql\sb50\sa50\cbpat11 {\f11\fs14\cf4 Refer to the TFL Designer 'GCDS Template Instructions' tab, under the 'Data Presentation' heading, for 'Adverse Events Tables Programming Notes'; these notes contain example tables for points 17 and 18, below, with the logic for analysis counts.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 }\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 GENERAL:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 1. The rows presented in the Overall AE Summary table should match the AE outputs presented in the study. A row for Death ADSL.DTHFL is required in the Overall AE Summary table unless a separate Death summary table is presented in the study.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 2. If the Overall AE Summary table is generated using a Subgroup analysis, then each category of the subgroup will displayed on a separate page as the first row of that page.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 3. For TEAEs of interest, optional rows may be added to the Overall AE Summary table. However, for multiple categories of TEAEs of interest a separate Overall AE Summary table for TEAEs of interest may be used, then each category of interest will be displayed on a separate page as the first row of that page.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 4. Use the Safety ADSL.SAFFL Analysis Set for Adverse Event tables.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 5. Only TEAEs will be summarized unless otherwise specified; TEAEs will be defined as any AEs that occurred on or after the first study drug dosing date and up to \u123?XX\u125? days \u123?or study drug-specific therapeutic reach\u125? after the date of the last dose of the study drug [and prior to the day of initiation of subsequent anticancer/antiviral/etc. therapy], unless otherwise specified. For interim analyses, refer to SAP for participants who are ongoing on study drug.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 6. If the onset date of the AE is incomplete and the AE stop date is not prior to the first dosing date of study drug, then the month and year (or year alone if month is not recorded) of onset determine whether an AE is treatment emergent. The event is considered treatment emergent if both of the following 2 criteria are met:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4    \u8226? The AE onset is the same as or after the month and year (or year) of the first dosing date of study drug, and}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4    \u8226? The AE onset date is the same as or before the month and year (or year) of the date corresponding to \u123?XX\u125? days \u123?or study drug-specific therapeutic reach\u125? after the date of the last dose of study drug [and prior to the day of initiation of subsequent anticancer/antiviral/etc. therapy].}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 An AE with completely missing onset and stop dates, or with the onset date missing and a stop date later than the first dosing date of study drug, will be considered to be treatment emergent. In addition, an AE with the onset date missing and incomplete stop date with the same or later month and year (or year alone if month is not recorded) as the first dosing date of study drug will be considered treatment emergent.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 7. Default sort order is alphabetically for SOCs [and HLT within SOC,] and then descending frequency of PTs in the total column. Summaries that include PT only, sort order is by descending frequency of PTs in the total column. Optionally, a different sort order maybe specified as based on the study design.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 8. For studies that collect adverse event data for individual study drugs, the layout may be altered to summarize the individual study drugs separately.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 9. A total column may be presented for studies where different doses of the same study drug are displayed.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 10. Rows may be added to summarize the number of participants with missing data, as applicable.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 11. Lower severity grades may be excluded from table summaries, as applicable.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 12. A P value may be displayed if pre-specified in the SAP. Display P values in a column if 2 treatment groups are shown in the table, or in a row if more than 2 treatment groups are shown.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 13. For Oncology studies, refer to the SAP when determining relevant custom grouping for lab abnormality AE terms (e.g., ADAE.AEDECOD are mapped: Neutrophil count decreased->Neutropenia, White blood cell count decreased->Leukopenia, Lymphocyte count decreased->Lymphopenia, Red blood cell count decreased->Anaemia, Platelet count decreased->Thrombocytopenia). Related footnote should be added to explain this.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 14. For studies where the analysis is based on the Treatment Emergent within each period, then in such instances the variable ADAE.TREMxxFL can be utilized to summarize the AE\u8217?s. [xx] in the variable name indicates each period and will be replaced by 01, 02, 03, etc.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 15. Rows for treatment mean difference and P value are optional for Exposure-Adjusted Incidence Rate (EAIR) summaries. Refer to the SAP when determining relevant statistical methods.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 16. For Oncology studies, the required displays are separate summaries of \u8216?TEAE with Grade 3 or 4\u8216? and \u8216?TEAE Leading to Death\u8217? (i.e., TEAE with Grade 5) instead of the combined summaries of \u8216?TEAE with Grade 3 or Higher\u8216?. For Virology and Inflammation studies, the preferred display is the combined summaries of \u8216?TEAE with Grade 3 or Higher\u8216? and separate summaries of \u8216?TEAE with Grade 3 or 4\u8216? and \u8216?TEAE Leading to Death\u8217? (i.e., TEAE with Grade 5) are optional only.}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 17. <Refer to 'Adverse Events Tables Programming Notes' in the 'GCDS Template Instructions' tab>}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 For Table 15.11.2.1.1 TEAE Overall Summary, the following rows are intended to count participants once only and at the highest severity grade experienced per participant throughout the study:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4    \u8226? TEAE with Grade 3 or 4}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4    \u8226? TEAE Leading to Death}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 If the highest severity grade experienced is a Grade 5, then those participants would be excluded from the \u8220?TEAE with Grade 3 or 4\u8221? row (but would be counted in the \u8220?TEAE Leading to Death\u8221? row).}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 For summaries related to study drug, subset records on relationship to study drug (ADAE.AREL=\u8217?RELATED\u8217?) first, before determining the highest severity grade experienced per participant. Participants are counted once only in the following rows at the highest severity grade experienced per participant of the drug-related TEAEs. If the highest severity grade of the drug-related TEAEs is a Grade 5, the participant is excluded from the \u8220?TEAE Related to Study Drug with Grade 3 or 4\u8221? row (but is counted in the \u8220?TEAE Related to Study Drug Leading to Death\u8221? row).}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4    \u8226? TEAE Related to Study Drug with Grade 3 or 4}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4    \u8226? TEAE Related to Study Drug Leading to Death}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 Example Study: In a 20-participant study, 20 participants have treatment-emergent maximum Grade 4 neutropenia and 2 participants have treatment-emergent maximum Grade 5 febrile neutropenia. All events are considered treatment-related except one case of Grade 5 febrile neutropenia. Refer the following summary table displays the expected participant counts:}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 18. <Refer to 'Adverse Events Tables Programming Notes' in the 'GCDS Template Instructions' tab>}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 For Table 15.11.2.2.2.1 Grade 3 or 4 TEAEs by SOC and PT, in the first summary row, include participants who experienced a maximum severity of Grade 3 or 4 throughout the study (ADAE.AOCCIFL=\u8217?Y\u8217? and ADAE.ATOXGRN in (3, 4)) and exclude participants who experienced a maximum severity of Grade 5 \u8211? this matches the \u8220?TEAE with Grade 3 or 4\u8221? row in the Overall Summary table. Subsequent rows for SOC, exclude participants who experienced Grade 5 when counting the highest severity grade within this SOC (ADAE.AOCCSIFL=\u8217?Y\u8217? and ADAE.ATOXGRN in (3, 4)). Subsequent rows for PT, exclude participants who experienced Grade 5 when counting the highest severity grade within this PT (ADAE.AOCCPIFL=\u8217?Y\u8217? and ADAE.ATOXGRN in (3, 4)).}\line {\f11\fs14\cf4 Additionally, for Table 15.11.2.3.3.1 Grade 3 or 4 Treatment-Related TEAEs by SOC and PT, subset the records on relationship to study drug (ADAE.AREL=\u8217?RELATED\u8217?) first, before determining the highest severity grade (i.e., Grade 3 or 4) per participant (first row \u8211? matches Overall Summary table) and for each SOC and PT when selecting records for the relevant 1st Max Sev./Int. and Related to Study Drug Occurrence Flag (ADAE.AOCCzzFL).}\par}
